{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37"],"question":"opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254 issue otelhttp error recording semantic conventions closed 2026-01-13","metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7470\\n\\nI also think that stabilization of https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans is a blocker for v1 of `otelhttp`. \\n\\n@open-telemetry/go-maintainers, do any thoughts or other proposals?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dashpole** — 2025-11-03T14:55:36Z\\n\\nWould your proposed guidlines be in-line with the current Development spec, or are you proposing something new?  If they are in-line with that spec, then SGTM.  Otherwise, I would prefer if you updated the spec first so our instrumentation libraries don't get out ahead of the spec.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-11-03T15:00:09Z\\n\\n> Would your proposed guidlines be in-line with the current Development spec, or are you proposing something new?\\n\\nI want them to be following the current semantic conventions that are in Development\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-02]\\n\\n# Issue: otelhttp: Cannot record error for spans when producing new semantic convention (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#7254)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254  \\n\\n**Author**: XSAM  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **Updated**: 2026-01-13T15:23:09Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelhttp  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **labeled** by XSAM `area: instrumentation`\\n\\n- 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **labeled** by XSAM `bug`\\n\\n- 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **labeled** by XSAM `instrumentation: otelhttp`\\n\\n- 2025-04-23T02:22:14Z · **renamed** by XSAM \\\"otelhttp: Cannot record error when producing new semantic convention\\\" → \\\"otelhttp: Cannot record error for spans when producing new semantic convention\\\"\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7470 i also think that stabil of http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on span is a blocker for v1 of otelhttp open telemetri go maintain do ani thought or other propos dashpol 2025 11 03t14 55 36z would your propos guidlin be in line with the current develop spec or are you propos someth new if they are in line with that spec then sgtm otherwis i would prefer if you updat the spec first so our instrument librari don t get out ahead of the spec pellar 2025 11 03t15 00 09z would your propos guidlin be in line with the current develop spec or are you propos someth new i want them to be follow the current semant convent that are in develop sourc id src issu 02 issu otelhttp can not record error for span when produc new semant convent open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 7254 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 author xsam creat 2025 04 23t02 21 22z updat 2026 01 13t15 23 09z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label bug area instrument instrument otelhttp mileston v1 400 timelin 2025 04 23t02 21 22z label by xsam area instrument 2025 04 23t02 21 22z label by xsam bug 2025 04 23t02 21 22z label by xsam instrument otelhttp 2025 04 23t02 22 14z renam by xsam otelhttp can not record error when produc new semant convent otelhttp can not record error for span when produc new semant convent\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"07f88ef62d2d32dc\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.45539518930056155, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2689192132865165, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8905058, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:13\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-02]\\n\\n# Issue: otelhttp: Cannot record error for spans when producing new semantic convention (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#7254)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254  \\n\\n**Author**: XSAM  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **Updated**: 2026-01-13T15:23:09Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelhttp  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n### Description\\n\\n`otelhttp` only uses `span.RecordError(err)` when `errType` is not empty\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8/instrumentation/net/http/otelhttp/transport.go#L132-L140\\n\\nBut `ErrorType` method never returns an empty attribute.\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8/instrumentation/net/http/httptrace/otelhttptrace/internal/semconv/httpconv.go#L443-L458\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nI don't have a preference on whether we should record `error.type` with `exception.type` at the same time. But the comment and the logic here seem conflicted. \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-02]\\n\\n# Issue: otelhttp: Cannot record error for spans when producing new semantic convention (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#7254)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254  \\n\\n**Author**: XSAM  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **Updated**: 2026-01-13T15:23:09Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelhttp  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (15)\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-04-23T08:03:12Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 02 issu otelhttp can not record error for span when produc new semant convent open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 7254 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 author xsam creat 2025 04 23t02 21 22z updat 2026 01 13t15 23 09z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label bug area instrument instrument otelhttp mileston v1 400 descript descript otelhttp onli us span recorderror err when errtyp is not empti http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8 instrument net http otelhttp transport go l132 l140 but errortyp method never return an empti attribut http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8 instrument net http httptrace otelhttptrac intern semconv httpconv go l443 l458 expect behavior i don t have a prefer on wheth