telemetri semant convent pull 3228 2026 01 12t17 33 42z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8386 2026 01 13t15 23 09z close by pellar 2026 04 27t06 41 51z cross referenc by coderabbitai bot http github com cento automot suit automot dev oper pull 260\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"dcb739467a1e76b9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.42670831998167097, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.24124301425953004, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8594607, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:13\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-06-16T07:44:04Z\\n\\nI created \\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7470\\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6904\\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6903\\n\\nI think it might be also good to add some \\\"error recording\\\" recommendations in https://pkg.go.dev/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace. However, we should first clarify it on the semantic conventions side.\\n\\n>  I believe [`span.RecordError`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/api.md#record-exception) remains valuable, particularly for **non-terminating errors**. A common use case is **retry logic**, where errors occur but don't immediately end the span. This is especially relevant in the context of **custom instrumentation**, where developers have full control and can explicitly record such intermediate errors.\\n\\nThis seems not compliant with https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-metrics\\n\\n> Errors that were retried or handled (allowing an operation to complete gracefully) SHOULD NOT be recorded on spans or metrics that describe this operation.\\n\\nCurrently, the only use case I see the only use of `span.RecordError` to use it for \\\"unhandled exceptions\\\" (which for Go can be done in the SDK) and to record multiple errors like here:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/9e39469c07651d62d1acd5155ddf9843c1b63436/instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go#L119-L124\\n\\nI do not find the semantic conventions clear and probably some work is also needed there.\\n\\nCC @lmolkova\\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-08-03T20:45:58Z\\n\\nSorry for joining the discussion late.\\n\\n@pellared I am confused about what we should do to handle errors, especially **non-terminating errors**. Should we do nothing if we encounter an error?\\n\\nFor instance, when facing code like this, do we do nothing for the error we receive?\\n\\n```go\\n\\nctx, span := tracer.Tracer(instrumentationName).Start(ctx, \\\"example\\\")\\n\\ndefer span.End()\\n\\nerr := query(ctx, db)\\n\\nif err != nil {\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"pellar 2025 06 16t07 44 04z i creat http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7470 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6904 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6903 i think it might be also good to add some error record recommend in http pkg go dev go opentelemetri io otel trace howev we should first clarifi it on the semant convent side i believ span recorderror http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif trace api md record except remain valuabl particular for non termin error a common use case is retri logic where error occur but don t immedi end the span this is especi relev in the context of custom instrument where develop have full control and can explicit record such intermedi error this seem not compliant with http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on metric error that were retri or handl allow an oper to complet grace should not be record on span or metric that describ this oper current the onli use case i see the onli use of span recorderror to use it for unhandl except which for go can be done in the sdk and to record multipl error like here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob 9e39469c07651d62d1acd5155ddf9843c1b63436 instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go l119 l124 i do not find the semant convent clear and probabl some work is also need there cc lmolkova xsam 2025 08 03t20 45 58z sorri for join the discuss late pellar i am confus about what we should do to handl error especi non termin error should we do noth if we encount an error for instanc when face code like this do we do noth for the error we receiv go ctx span tracer tracer instrumentationnam start ctx exampl defer span end err queri ctx db if err nil\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"4fdef9078d24ed37\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.37797187713974856, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18014081019964087, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8395777, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:13\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"} catch (Throwable e) {\\n\\n  span.recordException(e);\\n\\n  span.setAttribute(AttributeKey.stringKey(\\\"error.type\\\"), e.getClass().getCanonicalName())\\n\\n  span.setStatus(StatusCode.ERROR, e.getMessage());\\n\\n  throw e;\\n\\n} finally {\\n\\n  span.end();\\n\\n}\\n\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\nSo, a good start for us is to change the code from\\n\\n```go\\n\\n\\t\\t// set error type attribute if the error is part of the predefined\\n\\n\\t\\t// error types.\\n\\n\\t\\t// otherwise, record it as an exception\\n\\n\\t\\tif errType := t.semconv.ErrorType(err); errType.Valid() {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tspan.SetAttributes(errType)\\n\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tspan.RecordError(err)\\n\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\tspan.SetStatus(codes.Error, err.Error())\\n\\n```\\n\\nto\\n\\n```go\\n\\n\\t\\t// ErrorType should always return a valid error.type` for error\\n\\n\\t\\tspan.SetAttributes(t.semconv.ErrorType(err))\\n\\n\\t\\tspan.RecordError(err)\\n\\n\\t\\tspan.SetStatus(codes.Error, err.Error())\\n\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-06-11T12:24:35Z\\n\\nWhat is the value of recording the error as event if the type is set as attribute and value (`err.Error()`) as status description?\\n\\n> An exception SHOULD be recorded as an Event on the span during which it occurred if and only if it remains unhandled when the span ends and causes the span status to be set to ERROR.\\n\\nI argue that error result is not an exception. For me a `panic` that was not being recovered is an unhandled exception. We already cover this part of this specification here:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/blob/bc531cb3f9ce9c328b12e473b6409784728dc608/sdk/trace/span.go#L465-L482\\n\\nAdditionally see: https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans\\n\\nTherefore, we should not call `span.RecordError(err)`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dashpole** — 2025-06-12T17:03:33Z\\n\\n@pellared does that mean span.RecordError should essentially never be called by instrumentation, since panic recovery is already handled by the SDK?\\n\\nAlmost makes it seem like we should deprecate RecordError in the API, and document that End should handle recording exceptions for panics.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-06-13T07:21:05Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"catch throwabl e span recordexcept e span setattribut attributekey stringkey error type e getclass getcanonicalnam span setstatus statuscod error e getmessag throw e final span end so a good start for u is to chang the code from go set error type attribut if the error is part of the predefin error type otherwis record it a an except if errtyp t semconv errortyp err errtyp valid span setattribut errtyp els span recorderror err span setstatus code error err error to go errortyp should alway return a valid error type for error span setattribut t semconv errortyp err span recorderror err span setstatus code error err error pellar 2025 06 11t12 24 35z what is the valu of record the error a event if the type is set a attribut and valu err error a status descript an except should be record a an event on the span dure which it occur if and onli if it remain unhandl when the span end and caus the span status to be set to error i argu that error result is not an except for me a panic that wa not be recov is an unhandl except we alreadi cover this part of this specif here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go blob bc531cb3f9ce9c328b12e473b6409784728dc608 sdk trace span go l465 l482 addit see http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on span therefor we should not call span recorderror err dashpol 2025 06 12t17 03 33z pellar doe that mean span recorderror should essenti never be call by instrument sinc panic recoveri is alreadi handl by the sdk almost make it seem like we should deprec recorderror in the api and document that end should handl record except for panic pellar 2025 06 13t07 21 05z\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"5ba249bbec2363c0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3687398552532668, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17552811036180976, \"vector_similarity\": 0.81956726, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:13\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"\\treturn err\\n\\n}\\n\\nreturn nil\\n\\n```\\n\\nOr, should we record this error?\\n\\n```go\\n\\nctx, span := tracer.Tracer(instrumentationName).Start(ctx, \\\"example\\\")\\n\\ndefer span.End()\\n\\nerr := query(ctx, db)\\n\\nif err != nil {\\n\\n\\tspan.RecordError(err)\\n\\n\\treturn err\\n\\n}\\n\\nreturn nil\\n\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\nI don't think we should just ignore the error without recording it in the span. `RecordError` has `semconv.ExceptionMessage(err.Error())` to record error message, which is always useful when debugging.\\n\\nAre you trying to limit the usage of `RecordError` to only instrumentation? Why can the instrumentation record the error message?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-08-04T15:12:11Z\\n\\n> For instance, when facing code like this,\\n\\nIt looks like a **terminating** error to me which falls into https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans:\\n\\n> When the operation ends with an error, instrumentation:\\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-08-05T06:38:55Z\\n\\nI see. So, your proposal is\\n\\n```go\\n\\nctx, span := tracer.Tracer(instrumentationName).Start(ctx, \\\"example\\\")\\n\\ndefer span.End()\\n\\nerr := query(ctx, db)\\n\\nif err != nil {\\n\\n\\tspan.SetAttributes(semconv.ErrorType(err))\\n\\n\\tspan.SetStatus(codes.Error, err.Error())\\n\\n\\treturn err\\n\\n}\\n\\nreturn nil\\n\\n```\\n\\nIt makes sense.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-08-05T06:40:03Z\\n\\nCorrect \\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-08-05T06:50:03Z\\n\\n> In such cases, recording retry attempts as span events via span.RecordError gives users better visibility into transient issues without prematurely ending the span.\\n\\nWould it be strange to say we only record `exception` events when `panic` and retriable error happens? Retriable errors do not seem to be categorized as a type of `exception`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-11-03T13:34:57Z\\n\\nMy plan is to add OTel Go specfic \\\"recording errors\\\" guidelines into our [Style Guide](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#style-guide). Maybe it should be part of some more public user-facing docs like https://pkg.go.dev/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace. However, I prefer first trying it out more internally. One of the reasons is that https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans is \\\"Development\\\" and would need to be \\\"Stable\\\" first. I would work on it on the scope of:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"return err return nil or should we record this error go ctx span tracer tracer instrumentationnam start ctx exampl defer span end err queri ctx db if err nil span recorderror err return err return nil i don t think we should just ignor the error without record it in the span recorderror ha semconv exceptionmessag err error to record error messag which is alway use when debug are you tri to limit the usag of recorderror to onli instrument whi can the instrument record the error messag pellar 2025 08 04t15 12 11z for instanc when face code like this it look like a termin error to me which fall into http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on span when the oper end with an error instrument xsam 2025 08 05t06 38 55z i see so your propos is go ctx span tracer tracer instrumentationnam start ctx exampl defer span end err queri ctx db if err nil span setattribut semconv errortyp err span setstatus code error err error return err return nil it make sens pellar 2025 08 05t06 40 03z correct xsam 2025 08 05t06 50 03z in such case record retri attempt a span event via span recorderror give user better visibl into transient issu without prematur end the span would it be strang to say we onli record except event when panic and retriabl error happen retriabl error do not seem to be categor a a type of except pellar 2025 11 03t13 34 57z my plan is to add otel go specfic record error guidelin into our style guid http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go blob main contribut md style guid mayb it should be part of some more public user face doc like http pkg go dev go opentelemetri io otel trace howev i prefer first tri it out more intern one of the reason is that http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on span is develop and would need to be stabl first i would work on it on the scope of\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"306f7750594f646b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3638690874803033, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16630271068614758, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8248573, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:13\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I don't know what was the intent there. But it feels like `ErroTypeOther` should be the case where we want to fallback to recording an error?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-04-23T16:07:50Z\\n\\n> But it feels like ErroTypeOther should be the case where we want to fallback to recording an error?\\n\\nI don't find a way to make it return `ErrorTypeOther`. In most cases, it returns `semconv.ErrorTypeKey.String(\\\"*errors.errorString\\\")`.\\n\\nFor instance, errors created by `errors.New()` like `driver.ErrBadConn`. The type is `*errors.errorString`.\\n\\nI know it is difficult (or impossible) to get this via reflect, but do you think returning `semconv.ErrorTypeKey.String(\\\"database/sql/driver.ErrBadConn\\\")` is the ideal result for `driver.ErrBadConn`?\\n\\n> where we want to fallback to recording an error?\\n\\nI feel we should always make span recording the error, as this is the only way users can choose to record [`exception.message`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/4676c009fa6b8f4ed7d2321c991024373e77428e/docs/attributes-registry/exception.md#exception-message) and [`exception.stacktrace`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/4676c009fa6b8f4ed7d2321c991024373e77428e/docs/attributes-registry/exception.md#exception-stacktrace). While only know the error type does not seem to help a lot, these two attributes are very helpful when debugging.\\n\\n@open-telemetry/go-maintainers What do you think about this issue?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-04-24T18:26:30Z\\n\\nMore information: https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/trace/exceptions/ (not in the semconv doc)\\n\\nThe spec about exceptions says\\n\\n> An exception SHOULD be recorded as an Event on the span during which it occurred if and only if it remains unhandled **when the span ends and causes the span status to be set to ERROR**.\\n\\nIt even has a pseudo code that sets the `error.type` attribute for spans and calls `recordException` at the same time.\\n\\n```java\\n\\nSpan span = myTracer.startSpan(/*...*/);\\n\\ntry {\\n\\n  // Code that does the actual work which the Span represents\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i don t know what wa the intent there but it feel like errotypeoth should be the case where we want to fallback to record an error xsam 2025 04 23t16 07 50z but it feel like errotypeoth should be the case where we want to fallback to record an error i don t find a way to make it return errortypeoth in most case it return semconv errortypekey string error errorstr for instanc error creat by error new like driver errbadconn the type is error errorstr i know it is difficult or imposs to get this via reflect but do you think return semconv errortypekey string databas sql driver errbadconn is the ideal result for driver errbadconn where we want to fallback to record an error i feel we should alway make span record the error a this is the onli way user can choos to record except messag http github com open telemetri semant convent blob 4676c009fa6b8f4ed7d2321c991024373e77428e doc attribut registri except md except messag and except stacktrac http github com open telemetri semant convent blob 4676c009fa6b8f4ed7d2321c991024373e77428e doc attribut registri except md except stacktrac while onli know the error type doe not seem to help a lot these two attribut are veri help when debug open telemetri go maintain what do you think about this issu xsam 2025 04 24t18 26 30z more inform http opentelemetri io doc spec otel trace except not in the semconv doc the spec about except say an except should be record a an event on the span dure which it occur if and onli if it remain unhandl when the span end and caus the span status to be set to error it even ha a pseudo code that set the error type attribut for span and call recordexcept at the same time java span span mytrac startspan tri code that doe the actual work which the span repres\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"acde131f811068d7\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3615128274803033, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16630271068614758, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8170031, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:13\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"My proposal is to not use `span.RecordError` for **terminating errors** per [recording errors on spans semantic conventions](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans).\\n\\nDuring the SIG meeting, it was also noted that `span.RecordError` captures a stack trace. However, since the stack trace reflects where the error was recorded, not where it originated, I don’t find it particularly valuable. Additionally, capturing and emitting a stack trace has a performance cost. In most languages with exception handling (such as Java or .NET), the stack trace is already included in the thrown exception so the cost of capturing the stack trace was already taken and the stack trace is taken in the place where the exception was thrown.\\n\\n> @pellared does that mean span.RecordError should essentially never be called by instrumentation, since panic recovery is already handled by the SDK? Almost makes it seem like we should deprecate RecordError in the API,\\n\\nI believe [`span.RecordError`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/api.md#record-exception) remains valuable, particularly for **non-terminating errors**. A common use case is **retry logic**, where errors occur but don't immediately end the span. This is especially relevant in the context of **custom instrumentation**, where developers have full control and can explicitly record such intermediate errors.\\n\\nWhile instrumentation libraries typically just return errors, they could also benefit from `span.RecordError` if the underlying library provides hooks into retry or failure logic. In such cases, recording retry attempts as span events via `span.RecordError` gives users better visibility into transient issues **without prematurely ending the span**.\\n\\nFor these reasons, I don’t think `span.RecordError` should be deprecated. It might be worth capturing these use cases in the [error recording semantic conventions](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md) (cc @lmolkova).\\n\\nSide note: There is an OTEP https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/pull/4333 that proposes to record exceptions/errors as log records instead of span events.\\n\\n>  and document that End should handle recording exceptions for panics.\\n\\nI think that documenting that `span.End` should handle recording exceptions for panics is a good idea.\\n\\nIn my opinion, this is how we implement [recording an exception](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/exceptions.md#recording-an-exception) in the most possible user-friendly way.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"my propos is to not use span recorderror for termin error per record error on span semant convent http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on span dure the sig meet it wa also note that span recorderror captur a stack trace howev sinc the stack trace reflect where the error wa record not where it origin i don t find it particular valuabl addit captur and emit a stack trace ha a perform cost in most languag with except handl such a java or net the stack trace is alreadi includ in the thrown except so the cost of captur the stack trace wa alreadi taken and the stack trace is taken in the place where the except wa thrown pellar doe that mean span recorderror should essenti never be call by instrument sinc panic recoveri is alreadi handl by the sdk almost make it seem like we should deprec recorderror in the api i believ span recorderror http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif trace api md record except remain valuabl particular for non termin error a common use case is retri logic where error occur but don t immedi end the span this is especi relev in the context of custom instrument where develop have full control and can explicit record such intermedi error while instrument librari typic just return error they could also benefit from span recorderror if the under librari provid hook into retri or failur logic in such case record retri attempt a span event via span recorderror give user better visibl into transient issu without prematur end the span for these reason i don t think span recorderror should be deprec it might be worth captur these use case in the error record semant convent http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md cc lmolkova side note there is an otep http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif pull 4333 that propos to record except error a log record instead of span event and document that end should handl record except for panic i think that document that span end should handl record except for panic is a good idea in my opinion this is how we implement record an except http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif trace except md record an except in the most possibl user friend way\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"12b3633dd54dd417\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3588874374803033, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16630271068614758, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8082518, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074434348a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:13\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- 2025-07-02T08:06:06Z · **cross-referenced** by dmathieu ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7541\\n\\n- 2025-07-02T15:30:57Z · **cross-referenced** by flc1125 ← https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455\\n\\n- 2025-11-03T09:18:09Z · **cross-referenced** by pellared ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648\\n\\n- 2026-01-16T17:41:03Z · **cross-referenced** by MrAlias ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8419\\n\\n- 2026-04-21T06:02:25Z · **cross-referenced** by SAY-5 ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8851\\n\\n- 2026-05-31T02:40:32Z · **referenced** by SAY-5\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"2025 07 02t08 06 06z cross referenc by dmathieu http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7541 2025 07 02t15 30 57z cross referenc by flc1125 http github com golang go issu 74455 2025 11 03t09 18 09z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 2026 01 16t17 41 03z cross referenc by mralia http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8419 2026 04 21t06 02 25z cross referenc by say 5 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8851 2026 05 31t02 40 32z referenc by say 5\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074abb7e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"d8ffda2f6576ca9a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3480587393788128, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13961035625544693, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8344383, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074abb7e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:04\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Seek more engagement from gRPC; attempt in-person conversations at KubeCon if possible. David will sync with Josh on outreach.\\n\\n- Conclusion: Not likely to stabilize this year; set a goal to finalize a strategy next year once semconv progress is clearer.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [Stabilization of otelgrpc](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8078)?\\n\\n  - Related: [https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/8265](https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/8265)  \\n\\n  - We need the semconv to stabilize  \\n\\n  - There needs to be involvement from gRPC to progress this  \\n\\n  - [David] Update: I’m told that the SIG is active and is working towards stabilization. Not sure if gRPC is involved.  \\n\\n### Stabilization of otelhttp\\n\\n- Damien proposed starting an API audit for otelhttp to move towards stabilization.\\n\\n- A known bug (issue #7254) may be the only blocker; it’s a behavioral change around how errors are marked (events vs attributes) and interacts with semconv/spec wording.\\n\\n- Agreement:\\n\\n  - Begin the API review.\\n\\n  - Robert will take ownership of #7254 and draft a document clarifying interpretation and proposed resolution.\\n\\n  - The existence of bugs does not inherently block stabilization; they can be fixed post-stabilization if changes are non-breaking or properly versioned.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- Blocker (only one I think): [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254)  \\n\\n### OTel Explorer Go docs\\n\\n- Mike outlined a project to revamp the OTEL registry/explorer with a schema that documents spans/metrics emitted by instrumentations, aiming to render via Hugo and enable static analysis across Go SDKs and contrib modules.\\n\\n- Tyler’s feedback:\\n\\n  - Strong requirement: align schema with semantic conventions and ensure it’s compatible with Weaver (to enable validation and transformations across versions).\\n\\n  - Consider providing a JSON Schema (or CUE) for validation and potentially linking to existing semconv definitions to keep the spec concise.\\n\\n  - Scope can include eBPF/auto-instrumentation; representation should still fit the schema as long as it maps to OTEL signals.\\n\\n- Mike will iterate on the schema, explore Weaver integration, and coordinate with SIGs as needed.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n  - Context: [https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000](https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000)  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"seek more engag from grpc attempt in person convers at kubecon if possibl david will sync with josh on outreach conclus not like to stabil this year set a goal to final a strategi next year onc semconv progress is clearer refer stabil of otelgrpc http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8078 relat http github com grpc grpc go issu 8265 http github com grpc grpc go issu 8265 we need the semconv to stabil there need to be involv from grpc to progress this david updat i m told that the sig is activ and is work toward stabil not sure if grpc is involv stabil of otelhttp damien propos start an api audit for otelhttp to move toward stabil a known bug issu 7254 may be the onli blocker it s a behavior chang around how error are mark event v attribut and interact with semconv spec word agreement begin the api review robert will take ownership of 7254 and draft a document clarifi interpret and propos resolut the exist of bug doe not inher block stabil they can be fix post stabil if chang are non break or proper version refer blocker onli one i think http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 otel explor go doc mike outlin a project to revamp the otel registri explor with a schema that document span metric emit by instrument aim to render via hugo and enabl static analysi across go sdks and contrib modul tyler s feedback strong requir align schema with semant convent and ensur it s compat with weaver to enabl valid and transform across version consid provid a json schema or cue for valid and potenti link to exist semconv definit to keep the spec concis scope can includ ebpf auto instrument represent should still fit the schema a long a it map to otel signal mike will iter on the schema explor weaver integr and coordin with sig a need refer context http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073f05c28a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"c1daea2fff59ca3c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34512928582448044, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15790789403497213, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7819792, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073f05c28a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:18\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254 issue otelhttp error recording semantic conventions closed 2026-01-13\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"Issue **#7254 is closed as completed** (closed 2026-01-13) and was tracked under milestone **v1.40.0**. The authoritative work state marks the otelhttp error-recording task complete, but **does not establish a release containing the resolution**.\n\nThe issue concerned inconsistent behavior under the new conventions: `error.type` was set while `span.RecordError(err)` was not reached. Discussion centered on whether terminating errors should be represented as events or attributes, pending semantic-convention clarification.  \nRecords: `WS-05: Contrib Modules` (`T002`), `SRC-ISSUE-02`."}}
